### 3. Additional context:
Inclusion criteria strictly required: (1) Randomised Controlled Trial (RCT) design, (2) Population of healthcare 
students (medical, nursing, psychology, social work, etc.) aged 18+, (3) Psychological intervention targeting 
resilience, hardiness, or post-traumatic growth, (4) Comparison group (no intervention, waitlist, usual care, or active 
control), and (5) Relevant outcomes (resilience, anxiety, depression, stress, well-being, or quality of life).

Only two studies met all criteria:
- Study 254: Cluster-RCT evaluating Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction (MBSR) in medical students during clinical 
clerkships.
- Study 270: RCT evaluating resource-oriented coaching for examination-related stress in medical students.

All other studies were excluded primarily due to: non-RCT designs (systematic reviews, meta-analyses, cross-sectional 
surveys, longitudinal cohorts, quasi-experimental designs, psychometric validations, or theoretical papers), incorrect 
populations (general public, veterans, patients with specific diseases, non-healthcare college students, or practicing 
professionals), or mismatched abstracts. Decisions were made conservatively, but strict adherence to the RCT and 
healthcare student criteria resulted in the high exclusion rate.
