│ experienced significant positive improvements in mental distress, study stress, subjective well-being and            │
│ mindfulness after participating in the MBSR programme. TRIAL REGISTRATION NCT00892138."}, {"study_index": 308,       │
│ "title": "Resilience and return-to-work pain interventions: systematic review", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Resilience   │
│ is a developing concept in relation to pain, but has not yet been reviewed in return-to-work (RTW) contexts. AIMS To │
│ explore the role of resilience enhancement in promoting work participation for chronic pain sufferers, by reviewing  │
│ the effectiveness of existing interventions. METHODS Resilience was operationalized as: self-efficacy, active        │
│ coping, positive affect, positive growth, positive reinforcement, optimism, purpose in life and acceptance. Five     │
