consisted of eight weekly 1-hour individual sessions. Outcomes included measures of problem-solving skill and negative 
affectivity. RESULTS There were no significant between-group differences at baseline (T1). Except for level of 
problem-solving skill, which was directly taught in the PSST arm, outcome measures improved equally in both groups 
immediately postintervention (T2). However, at the 3-month follow-up (T3), mothers in the PSST group continued to show 
significant improvements in mood, anxiety, and post-traumatic stress; mothers in the NDS group showed no further 
